#
# prima-materia — the Ra material, entered at The Law of One, Book I
#
# Opened from the structure-driven entrance of SPEC §14: pmt:RaMaterial was
# registered at pm:corpusNamed in traditions/registry-channeled.ttl with no
# node. The registration names the five books and the L/L Research session
# transcripts. What was opened is Book I, The Ra Material, in the L/L
# Research print of 1984: the introduction by Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty,
# the photographs and their captions, and sessions 1 to 26 (January 15 to
# February 17, 1981), read complete in a full-text layer of that edition.
# Books II to V are unopened and the work nodes say so.
#
# Order of the file: the works; the tradition with the three decisions; then
# the harvest in the order of the work, the introduction and sessions 1 to 8
# first, sessions 9 to 26 after, each session under its own heading.
#
# Citation. The questions are not numbered in this edition; nodes cite
# session, date and page. Page numbers stand at the foot of each page in the
# layer; missing and misread numerals were placed by sequence.
#
# Who speaks. A claim made by Ra is the work's claim. The introduction is by
# Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty and quotes earlier messages the group received
# from other contacts, chiefly one called Hatonn; their account of their own
# procedure and of earlier experiments is entered with the speaker named in
# the definition. A statement made only by the Questioner is entered only as a
# report of the group's own procedure or observation.
#
# Identifiers. Where the same term of the teaching is entered from both halves
# of the book, the node from sessions 9 to 26 carries the number of the session
# it starts from (pmc:RaHarvest and pmc:RaHarvestSession10): one doctrine, two
# places.
#

#
# The works
#

pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch I: Das Ra-Material"@de ;
    skos:note "Read complete on 2026-10-25 in The Law of One: Book I, The Ra Material, by Ra, An Humble Messenger of the Law of One, copyright 1984 by James Allen McCarty, Don Elkins and Carla Rueckert (Louisville: L/L Research), title page and copyright page in the full-text layer of archive.org the-ra-material-an-ancient-astronaut-speaks-by-don-elkins-james-allen-mc-carty-c, 500400 characters, ASCII letter share 1.0. The introduction (pp. 4-51), the photographs with their captions (pp. 52-68) and sessions 1 to 26 (pp. 70-233) were read complete in two halves, the introduction with sessions 1 to 8 and sessions 9 to 26, each by one reader writing the nodes from the wording. The library scan of the Donning print of 1984 (ramaterialancien00rasp) is lending-restricted and was not used."@en ;
    skos:note "The layer drops or misreads a number of page numerals, which were placed by sequence; the dates of sessions 9 and 10 read 'January tj' and are taken as January 27 from the sessions on either side; the text of footnote 3 on p. 232 is not in the layer. No stretch of running text is missing."@en ;
    skos:note "The book is the transcript of tape recordings of question and answer, and English is its original language, so the rule of two translations does not apply."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookTwo a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book II"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch II"@de ;
    skos:note "Sessions 27 to 50. Reachable: archive.org the-ra-material-the-law-of-one-v-1-5-don-elkins-carla-rueckert carries Books I to V in one full-text layer of about two million characters, without an imprint read. Not opened in this run, which took Book I complete instead of five books in part."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookThree a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book III"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch III"@de ;
    skos:note "Sessions 51 to 75. Reachable in the same full-text layer as Book II; not opened in this run."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFour a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book IV"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch IV"@de ;
    skos:note "Sessions 76 to 100. Reachable in the same full-text layer as Book II; not opened in this run. The registration places the examinable claims in the conditions of contact and the instrument's decline, which Books III to V carry at length."@en .

pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFive a dcterms:BibliographicResource ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of One, Book V: Personal Material"@en, "Das Gesetz des Einen, Buch V: Persönliches Material"@de ;
    skos:note "The fragments withheld from Books I to IV, with commentary by Rueckert and McCarty. Reachable in the same full-text layer as Book II; not opened in this run."@en .

#
# The tradition
#

pmt:RaMaterial a pm:Tradition ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    rdfs:label "The Ra material"@en, "Das Ra-Material"@de ;
    skos:definition "The transmission of one hundred and six sessions received between 1981 and 1984 by a group of three working in fixed roles, teaching a cosmology of densities, a choice between service to others and service to self, and a harvest at the close of a cycle."@en ;
    skos:note "The best documented reception in the block. Questioner, instrument and scribe are named, the sessions are numbered and dated, the working conditions are described including the instrument's physical decline, and the transmission continued under a different contact after this one ended. The cosmological claims are largely undecidable; the claims about the conditions of contact and about what the work cost the instrument are not, and that is where an examination would begin."@en ;
    skos:note "Contact route, the first of the three decisions SPEC §14 requires, kept at documented, and the route is printed in the work. The introduction describes nineteen years of the group's meditation and channelling before Ra, after the method of an earlier contactee group, with messages from a contact called Hatonn of the same Confederation that Ra names; Elkins sets his account in the physics of Dewey Larson; and when the Questioner reads out Oahspe's figure of fifty-one per cent service to others for harvest, Ra calls it correct. Agreement of this material with the contactee literature, with Theosophy or with Oahspe is reception along that route and counts once."@en ;
    skos:note "Recension and edition, the second decision: Book I in the L/L Research print of 1984, the transcript the group itself published, cited by session, date and page. The tapes and the later relistened transcripts of L/L Research were not compared; where a later edition corrects a word, the node does not know it."@en ;
    skos:note "The third decision, the number of citable places: Book I read complete, 368 nodes in the order of the work, 187 from the introduction and sessions 1 to 8 and 181 from sessions 9 to 26, each at a session and page."@en ;
    skos:note "Two counts, kept apart as SPEC §15 asks. Signs of success: twenty, eleven of them from the introduction (the reception of the group's channels, the bending of metal, psychic surgery, meditation) and nine from Ra (among them a life span near nine hundred years as the mark of a harmonious people, the feeling of being awakened in a wanderer, hope and friendly feeling as the marks of a positive contact). Conditions of failure: sixty-one. Twelve set a deadline, threshold or count: the 51 and 5 per cent of harvest, the 25,000-year cycle that strikes like a clock, an approximate harvest in 2011, life spans falling from 900 to 35-40 years, misalignments of the instrument's articles by 3, 1.4, 0.5 and 0.2 degrees, two sessions a day found too wearing. Forty-one name an outcome someone could notice. Where the failure is put: on the instrument thirteen times, on the hearer's free will ten, on the seeker's own orientation and practice and on the researcher's attitude most of the rest, on the Questioner's questions once, and never on discord in the group."@en ;
    skos:note "The finding the count carries. Three of the introduction's conditions of failure announce in advance that the phenomena will not appear under examination: desire for proof, rigorous controls and the analysis of specimens are each said to dampen or annul the effect (pmc:RaProofNullResults, pmc:RaRigorousControlsDampen, pmc:RaSpecimenAnalysisCaution). Ra's own observable failures in sessions 1 to 8 lie almost wholly on the instrument's body and the arrangement of the room, which is the examinable layer the registration pointed at. And the one disagreement inside the book is of that kind: Ra says the instrument can sustain two sessions a day, the introduction reports that two a day proved much too wearing (pmc:RaTwoSessionsDispute)."@en ;
    pm:principalCorpus "Elkins, Rueckert and McCarty, The Law of One, Books I to V; the L/L Research session transcripts" ;
    pm:corpusWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookTwo, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookThree, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFour, pmw:TheLawOfOneBookFive ;
    pm:coverageState pm:placesEntered ;
    pm:contactRoute pm:contactRouteDocumented ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 4-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .


#
# Introduction (Elkins, Rueckert, McCarty), pp. 4-51
#

pmc:RaContactReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The work's claim that its wording is Ra's, spoken through Carla Rueckert in trance"@en, "Die Behauptung des Werkes, sein Wortlaut sei der Ras, gesprochen durch Carla Rueckert in Trance"@de ;
    skos:definition "The claim the book makes about its own authorship. Elkins calls it an exact transcript from tape recordings of twenty-six sessions of an experiment designed to communicate with an extraterrestrial being, the race called Ra, by what he prefers to call tuned trance telepathy. The prefatory note to the sessions says the group began receiving a communication from the social memory complex Ra on January 15, 1981, and that the pages contain an exact transcript of the first twenty-six sessions, edited only to remove some personal material."@en ;
    skos:note "This node records the claim, not its truth. The title page names Ra as author, an humble messenger of the Law of One, and the copyright holders as McCarty, Elkins and Rueckert; the source lines here name the edition a reader can obtain. Rueckert says she does not know how the trance occurs, and Elkins classes her state as telepathic reception in the trance state."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "Carla L. Rueckert, the instrument, in trance; questions asked by Don Elkins, the questioner; transcription by James Allen McCarty" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Ra, which calls itself a social memory complex of those who are of the Law of One and an humble messenger of the Law of One; called by Elkins a sixth-density social memory complex" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "The contact began on January 15, 1981, three weeks after McCarty joined the group and a few days after Rueckert's first experience of trance, two sittings to contact a deceased friend. It came while she was working with an advanced meditation student, Leonard Cecil; she challenged the entity in the name of Christ, it remained, and she went almost immediately into trance. Before each session the group decided the night before, gave the instrument a half-hour back massage, meditated, performed a ritual of protection and cleansing of the room, laid her prone under a white blanket with her eyes covered and hooked up three tape recorder microphones below her chin; Elkins aligned the table bearing Bible, candle, incense and chalice of water with her head, and Elkins and McCarty walked the Circle of One. McCarty says she departs her physical body and Ra uses it to make the words; she has no memory of the session; Elkins calls her name until she responds. McCarty transcribed the tapes. The questions were prepared by all three and asked by Elkins." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 4-5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 47-51; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), prefatory note to the sessions, p. 69; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaTunedTranceTelepathy a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tuned trance telepathy: Elkins's name for the group's method of contact"@en, "Abgestimmte Trance-Telepathie: Elkins' Name für die Kontaktmethode der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elkins says the research group uses what he prefers to call tuned trance telepathy to communicate with an extraterrestrial race called Ra, in English because Ra knows it. Rueckert reports that Elkins, though he finds her trance similar to others he has observed, calls it telepathic reception in the trance state, and that neither she nor the others know how to aid her beyond a certain point in achieving it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 49; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHoaxCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Extreme caution before concluding: hoaxes and garbage data in paranormal research"@en, "Äußerste Vorsicht vor Schlüssen: Schwindel und Datenmüll in der paranormalen Forschung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elkins, after almost thirty years of research in so-called paranormal phenomena, recommends extreme caution in reaching a conclusion. Where it is possible to make money, gain notoriety or have fun by perpetrating a hoax, someone usually does it; paranormal and psychic areas are therefore prime targets for the trickster, and the careful researcher usually has to observe copious amounts of garbage data to find a possible imbedded gem of truth, especially in Philippine psychic surgery and in spirit communication in general. He says the book is not a treatise of his opinion, that his opinion may change at any time, and that only time will tell the accuracy of his best guess."@en ;
    skos:note "A caution the editors direct at their own field, including the channelling the book consists of."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaTunedTranceTelepathy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 4-5; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaVocalChanneling a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Vocal channelling: speaking the thoughts that come and analysing only afterwards"@en, "Stimmliches Channeln: die kommenden Gedanken aussprechen und erst danach prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The group sat meditating according to instructions in material Harold Price had brought from a Detroit group, which gave the means of generating further material from the same source without physical contact. Through the Detroit contactee Walter Rogers the group was instructed to refrain from analysis, to speak the thoughts, and to analyze the communication only after it had been completed. Rueckert describes her own practice as conscious channelling, using her free will to clothe telepathic concepts in her own language; in free will channelling one can choose to stop, and the channel never knows in advance what the next concept will be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 48-49; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTelepathicReception a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reception of transmissions by telepathic contact"@en, "Empfang von Übermittlungen durch telepathischen Kontakt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to receive transmissions, that is, to produce information by telepathic contact with a source held to be extraterrestrial, which the introduction reports for the members of Elkins's experimental group from 1962 and for receivers trained in later meetings. Hatonn, quoted in the introduction, says that those who receive the passed-on information will themselves be able to reach a state of thinking sufficiently in tune with the Confederation's vibrations to receive its contact, so that the process is self-generating."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 8; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVocalChannelingYieldsReception a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Speaking the thoughts without analysis yields reception within a month for half the group"@en, "Das Aussprechen der Gedanken ohne Prüfung bringt binnen eines Monats der halben Gruppe den Empfang"@de ;
    skos:definition "After the night the group was told to speak its thoughts, a month had not gone by before half the group had begun to produce information, and within a year all in the group except Rueckert were able to receive transmissions."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: half the group producing information within a month and all but one receiving within a year, a count the introduction gives itself."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaVocalChanneling ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaFearOfImproperWords a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Fear of not speaking the proper words blocks the instrument and slows the speech"@en, "Die Furcht, nicht die rechten Worte zu sprechen, blockiert das Instrument und verlangsamt die Rede"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the first six months, sitting meditating according to the instructions, everyone in the group except Rueckert made only strange noises with their mouths, guttural clicks, slurps and tongue flops. The visiting contactee was then told by telepathic impression that the members were being used as instruments of communication but were all blocked through fear that they would not be speaking the proper words. After the block was lifted the speech was slow and difficult at first, because each receiver wanted a precise impression of each and every word and in many cases wanted to be completely controlled for fear of making an error in transmission."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the fear of the wrong word is named as the block, and the wish for complete control as the cause of the slow speech; the outcomes, noises without words and then slow speech, are observable, and the failure is put on the instruments."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaVocalChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 6; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaProofNullResults a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A desire for proof leads to null results and voided experiments"@en, "Ein Verlangen nach Beweis führt zu Nullergebnissen und ungültigen Versuchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert says Elkins counts her great gullibility among her assets as a research associate: she takes things at face value and analyzes only afterwards, and she calls this a vital factor in obtaining good results in paranormal research. A desire for proof will inevitably lead to null results and voided experiments. An open mind, one willing to be gullible, leads to a subjective and personal certainty which does not equal proof, as it cannot be systematically reproduced in others; she calls this subjective knowing a central part of the spiritual evolution Ra speaks of."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the researcher's desire for proof is named as what produces null results; the outcome is observable, the cause is an attitude of the researcher. The same passage warns the reader that the certainty it offers is not proof."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaTunedTranceTelepathy ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 7; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMaterializationMediumship a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Materialization of spirits in a seance"@en, "Materialisation von Geistern in einer Séance"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert reports four demonstrations by the Spiritualist minister James Tingley in Toledo in 1971, whose concrete-block meeting place Elkins had examined inside and out and found without gadgets: ghost-like figures seen clearly, Elkins seeing even the strands of hair; a solid ghost known as Sister, whom Elkins later linked to his mother; and a Master who made the room grow very cold, touched Rueckert hard enough to bruise her arm so that she would know he was real, walked through the two of them, blessed the room, and pooled down on the floor and was gone. Elkins had sought such a materialization, one he himself could believe, because he thought seance materializations might be of the same nature as those of UFOs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 7-8; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaDailyMentalTuning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Daily meetings for intensive mental tuning"@en, "Tägliche Treffen zur intensiven geistigen Abstimmung"@de ;
    skos:definition "From 1974, after twelve years of listening, Elkins had Rueckert take up channelling seriously, and the two began a series of daily meetings designed to work intensively on her mental tuning; others from the Sunday night meditations joined them. During these intensive meditations the group began keeping the tape recorder going whenever a session started."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 8; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDailyMentalTuningYieldsReception a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Daily intensive meditation yields about a dozen new receivers in three months"@en, "Tägliche intensive Meditation bringt in drei Monaten etwa ein Dutzend neue Empfänger hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Within three months of the daily meetings the group generated about a dozen new telepathic receivers."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: about a dozen new receivers within three months."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaDailyMentalTuning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 8; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaHypnoticRegression a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Regressive hypnosis: age regression, lost time and previous lives"@en, "Regressive Hypnose: Altersregression, verlorene Zeit und frühere Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Regressive hypnosis as the group used it: Elkins's more than two hundred age regressions probing past the birth experience; the regression of UFO witnesses to recover the time they could not account for, after a lengthy induction to the proper state of concentration; and the separate regression of four subjects to a life on another planet, questioned by Elkins and the hypnotist Lawrence Allison."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 5; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 10-11; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 36-42; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPastLifeRecall a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recall under hypnosis of lost time and of previous incarnations"@en, "Erinnerung unter Hypnose an verlorene Zeit und frühere Inkarnationen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Recall under hypnosis of what the conscious mind does not hold. The introduction reports a nineteen-year-old who recovered thirty-eight lost minutes as an examination aboard a craft by three machine-like beings; Elkins's early investigations, which seemed to indicate that reincarnation was a probability and that incarnations contain situations and lessons more easily understood in the light of previous incarnations; and three women and one man who, separately regressed, gave independent and dovetailing accounts of one community on another planet, a temple, wordless communication and a life of study and meditation, the man adding technical detail."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 10-11; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 19; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 36-42; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHypnoticRegressionYieldsRecall a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Regressive hypnosis yields recall of lost time and previous lives"@en, "Regressive Hypnose bringt die Erinnerung an verlorene Zeit und frühere Leben hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The witness who wished to find his lost time was moved back under hypnosis to the moment beneath the craft and found himself inside it; the four subjects regressed to the other planet described its clothing, its temple, its music and its manner of speaking without words, and the man was brought through his death there and paused between incarnations to say why he had come to Earth: to help the people who are lost."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaHypnoticRegression ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaPastLifeRecall ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 10-11; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 36-42; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaRigorousControlsDampen a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Rigorous controls dampen the outcome of telepathic experiments"@en, "Strenge Kontrollen dämpfen den Ausgang telepathischer Versuche"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction says there has never been a definitive study proving good telepathic communication. Elkins states that his telepathic experiments with Uri Geller have been totally successful, but that they were deliberately not performed under rigorous scientific control and could not be included in any orthodox report; the authors give it as their opinion that rigorous controls have a dampening effect on the outcome of any experiment of this type. They keep the word alleged before telepathic communications from extraterrestrials because there is no way of proving the basic concept."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: controls are named as what dampens the outcome, so that a null result under control is announced in advance as an effect of the control rather than of the claim; the failure is put on the experimental conditions. The introduction later cites John Taylor's controlled experiments with children as good solid data (p. 18), so the authors hold both positions; one voice, not entered as a dispute."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 11-12; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMetalBendingByWanting a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling metal to bend without touching it forcefully"@en, "Metall heißen, sich zu biegen, ohne es kräftig zu berühren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Elkins, on the telephone with a fourteen-year-old who had had a UFO encounter, asked him to take a piece of silverware and tell it to bend without touching it in any firm or forceful way. The introduction also reports children who, after watching Uri Geller on television, cause bends and breaks in metal and other materials just by wanting the break or bend to occur."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 12; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMentalMetalBending a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Action at a distance by the mind: bending and breaking metal by wanting it"@en, "Fernwirkung durch den Geist: Metall durch Wollen biegen und brechen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Action at a distance as a function of mind, specifically the will, which the introduction says the physics Ra discusses posits: the bending and breaking of metal and plastic objects without force, done mostly by children and increasing in number daily, including objects sealed in glass cylinders by a glass blower in John Taylor's experiments with about fifty children. Rueckert says the reader of the Ra material will discover why it is mostly children who can do this and what it has to do with the rest of the UFO message."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 12-13; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 18; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMetalBendingYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Telling the fork to bend yields the bend"@en, "Die Gabel heißen, sich zu biegen, bringt die Biegung hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The boy picked up a fork, did as Elkins suggested, and the fork immediately bent nearly double; he was so startled that he would not come back to the telephone. Under Taylor's controlled circumstances the children were still able to bend and break multitudinous objects."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the fork bent nearly double at once; under seal, the objects bent and broke."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMetalBendingByWanting ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaMentalMetalBending ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 12-13; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaHigherSelfInquiry a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Asking the Higher Self under hypnosis whether the lesson is learned"@en, "Das höhere Selbst unter Hypnose fragen, ob die Lektion gelernt ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a previous life had been discussed and while the subject was still in trance, the hypnotist Lawrence Allison asked him, as he often did, to contact what is loosely referred to as his Higher Self, and had him ask whether the lesson of that life had been learned and whether, since it had, the symptom tied to it could be healed as no longer necessary."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 19; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHigherSelfNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "The Higher Self, consulted under hypnosis"@en, "Das höhere Selbst, unter Hypnose befragt"@de ;
    skos:definition "What the hypnotist loosely calls the subject's Higher Self is asked through the subject in trance and answers: it says the lesson has been learned and agrees that the allergy may be healed."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Higher Self" ;
    pm:nameRole "the subject's own higher self, reached through the subject under hypnosis and able to judge whether a lesson is learned and to consent to a healing" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 19; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLessonLearning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lessons chosen before incarnation, to be learned and not avoided"@en, "Vor der Inkarnation gewählte Lektionen, zu lernen und nicht zu umgehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn, quoted in the introduction, says that at incarnation each was aware that certain lessons hitherto unlearned were to be the goals of this incarnation; a life that seems a series of difficulties of one particular type points to one of them; they are not to be avoided but learned. Rueckert says the lessons are always along the lines of how to love better, more fully, more deeply or with more kindness, and that each entity's are unique; the introduction's allergy case speaks of the lesson of putting people first."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 31-32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHigherSelfHealing a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Healing of a condition whose lesson has been learned, by the Higher Self's consent"@en, "Heilung eines Leidens, dessen Lektion gelernt ist, mit Zustimmung des höheren Selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "A boy whose allergies to all living things kept him from cutting grass, smelling flowers or going outside in the blooming season was regressed to a life as a solitary English landowner who avoided all human contact and whose one pleasure was his garden. His Higher Self said the lesson of putting people first had been learned and agreed that the allergy could be healed, since it was no longer necessary. Rueckert gives it as an example of the relationship some call karma."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHigherSelfInquiryYieldsHealing a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Asking the Higher Self yields the cure of the allergy"@en, "Die Befragung des höheren Selbst bringt die Heilung der Allergie hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The hypnotist brought the boy out of trance, scraped magnolia pollen from his piano and blew it directly at the boy's nose. The boy protested that he was allergic; the hypnotist answered that he did not hear him sneezing. The boy remained cured of his allergy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: no sneeze at the pollen, and the cure lasting."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaHigherSelfInquiry ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaHigherSelfHealing ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLessonBeforeHealing a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The lesson learned before the symptom is healed"@en, "Die Lektion gelernt, bevor das Symptom geheilt wird"@de ;
    skos:definition "The healing was asked for on the ground that the lesson had been learned and the allergy was therefore no longer necessary; the Higher Self was asked first whether the lesson had been learned and only then whether the allergy could be healed."@en ;
    skos:note "Prescribed order and not stated necessity: the account gives the learned lesson as the reason for the healing and does not say what happens when the healing is asked for first."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaHigherSelfHealing ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaLessonLearning ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 19-20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMagicalPersonalityWork a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Work upon the magical personality: interiorizing, accepting responsibility, balancing reactions"@en, "Arbeit an der magischen Persönlichkeit: verinnerlichen, Verantwortung übernehmen, Reaktionen ausgleichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert describes a study of the so-called magical personality: by interiorizing experience, by accepting responsibility for all that occurs, by carefully analyzing one's reactions to all that occurs, and by eventually balancing those reactions so that one's actions are generated within the self and are no longer simple reactions to outward stimulus. Each time a person sustains an unfortunate situation and reacts by not giving anger for anger or sadness for sadness but by offering compassion and comfort where none was expected, the thread of inner strength is strengthened."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMagicalPersonality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The magical personality and the art of causing changes in consciousness at will"@en, "Die magische Persönlichkeit und die Kunst, Veränderungen des Bewusstseins nach Willen zu bewirken"@de ;
    skos:definition "A thread that runs through daily life which can be grasped and used to remove oneself from time to time into a framework in which reality is seen as that of the spiritual body, the personality that exists from incarnation to incarnation. Strengthened, it gives some small claim to the art of causing changes in consciousness at will, which Rueckert calls the classic definition of magic, and associates one more and more with a life closely related to the organic evolution of the universe."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMagicalPersonalityWorkYields a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Work upon the magical personality yields a small claim to magic"@en, "Die Arbeit an der magischen Persönlichkeit bringt einen kleinen Anspruch auf Magie hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "By working upon the magical personality in these ways we strengthen it until we are able to have some small claim to the art of causing changes in consciousness at will."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMagicalPersonalityWork ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaMagicalPersonality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 20; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHatonnReceiving a pm:Receiving ;
    rdfs:label "The introduction's claim that its quoted messages come from Hatonn through the group's channels"@en, "Die Behauptung der Einleitung, ihre zitierten Botschaften stammten von Hatonn durch die Kanäle der Gruppe"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction quotes at length messages received in the group's meetings and attributes them to an entity called Hatonn, of the Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator, who has spoken with the group and several others for many years."@en ;
    skos:note "The receiver is deliberately unnamed, which is itself a finding about this witness: the shape asks for the person through whom the wording came, and the work withholds it on principle. One quoted passage says my voice is now the voice of this instrument, my thoughts are her thoughts, so at least that receiver was a woman."@en ;
    pm:receivedBy "unnamed vocal channels of the Louisville meditation group; the introduction says the group never describes who the receiver was" ;
    pm:claimedSpeaker "Hatonn, of the Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator, speaking from a craft above the group" ;
    pm:receptionCircumstance "Messages received in the group's meditation meetings, held in Louisville since 1962 and taped since 1974, through members trained as vocal channels; the introduction quotes transcripts and marks breaks between transcripts with a symbol, and gives as its reason for naming no receiver that the information matters rather than the person transmitting." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 22; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHatonnNaming a pm:Naming ;
    rdfs:label "Hatonn, a Confederation entity speaking through the group"@en, "Hatonn, ein Wesen der Konföderation, das durch die Gruppe spricht"@de ;
    skos:definition "An entity called Hatonn, who has spoken with the group and several others for many years, says that the purpose of at least some of the UFOs seen at this time is a desire to be of service, that he is in a craft far above the group's dwelling and able to monitor its thoughts, which the Confederation does not consider an infringement since it sees these thoughts as its own and as the Creator's, and that the Confederation are the Harvesters."@en ;
    pm:nameForm "Hatonn" ;
    pm:nameRole "a member entity of the Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator, in a craft above the Earth, speaking through vocal channels" ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaConfederation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Confederation of Planets in the Service of the Infinite Creator"@en, "Die Konföderation der Planeten im Dienst des Unendlichen Schöpfers"@de ;
    skos:definition "The name used by Hatonn and by Ra. Ra counts approximately fifty-three civilizations comprising approximately five hundred planetary consciousness complexes, among them those from this planet who have attained dimensions beyond the third, planetary entities within this solar system and planetary entities from other galaxies; a true confederation in that its members are not alike but allied in service according to the Law of One. Its members wait for the calling. Hatonn says they have contacted the people of Earth at intervals of thousands of years, those who sought their aid, and are very sorry they cannot step upon the soil and teach."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 101-102; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVibratoryRate a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The vibration or vibratory rate of the individual"@en, "Die Schwingung oder Schwingungsrate des Einzelnen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says that the receiver must become of a certain vibration as a result of his thinking, that the channels' verbal communications create a system of thought and a desire for spiritual awareness that raises his vibration, and that the choice each person makes is measured by his vibratory rate, which motivation from within increases and proof imposed from without does not."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 34-35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVibrationBeforeContact a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A certain vibration first, then contact: raised by thinking, speeded by groups, finished in meditation"@en, "Erst eine bestimmte Schwingung, dann der Kontakt: durch Denken gehoben, durch Gruppen beschleunigt, in der Meditation vollendet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: for this is how contacts work. It is first necessary, if the entity is to be able to receive our contact, for him to become of a certain vibration as a result of his thinking. This is greatly speeded by involvement in groups such as this, and it is finally done through meditation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a receiver who has not reached the vibration cannot receive the contact; no threshold is given and the failure is put on the receiver's thinking."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaTelepathicReception ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaVibratoryRate ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "The entity is not able to receive the contact: it is first necessary, if the entity is to be able to receive our contact, for him to become of a certain vibration." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 22-23; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTruthWithoutProof a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Truth offered without proof: imposed or proven, it would have no usable effect"@en, "Wahrheit ohne Beweis angeboten: aufgezwungen oder bewiesen, hätte sie keine brauchbare Wirkung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says the Confederation cannot step upon the soil and teach, for this would be a very great disservice to those who do not desire its service, and would have little effect even on those who desire it, since understanding comes from within; its very utterance would be accepted by many as valid, and it does not wish to be thought the ultimate representative of the Creator's truth. Truth must be realized from within and cannot be impressed from without; the Confederation remains in hiding because it cannot serve one individual and at the same time do a disservice to his neighbour by proving within his own mind that it exists. It offers truth without proof, so that the motivation comes from within and the vibratory rate is increased; an offering of proof, or an impressing of truth such that one would be forced to accept it, would have no usable effect upon his vibratory rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: forced acceptance and proof are named as having no usable effect on the vibratory rate; the outcome is not observable, and the failure is put on the hearer's free will. A caution that also explains in advance why no proof will be given."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaVibratoryRate ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 23; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 28; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaOriginalThought a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The original thought: love as the unity in which each sees the other as the Creator"@en, "Der ursprüngliche Gedanke: Liebe als die Einheit, in der jeder den anderen als den Schöpfer sieht"@de ;
    skos:definition "What members of the Confederation call the original thought, which Rueckert glosses as love implying a unity so great that we see each other and ourselves as the Creator and so see one being; she calls it the very heart of telepathy. Hatonn says all thought that is generated is generated by the Creator, whose infinite parts all have free will, and that man on Earth has become isolated in his thinking from the concept that permeates most of the creation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 23-24; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMeditation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation as the Confederation messages ask for it"@en, "Meditation, wie die Botschaften der Konföderation sie verlangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Meditation, always suggested in the contactee messages as the best means of attaining understanding, of progressing spiritually and of understanding the nature and purpose of the illusion. Hatonn says it stills the active conscious mind, which is continually seeking stimulus within the illusion; that it begins as a simple process and little by little becomes a way in which one lives; and that the Confederation cannot overemphasize its importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: the introduction says the seeker's state of mind has the opportunity of being continuously in a far more pleasant configuration than that of one not seeking."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 25-27; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 29-30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaAppreciationOfReality a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Appreciation of reality: the illusion of separation reduced to a total illusion"@en, "Wertschätzung der Wirklichkeit: die Illusion der Trennung auf eine völlige Illusion zurückgeführt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The return to an appreciation of reality, of the functioning of the real creation, rather than of the illusion created by man's mind; Hatonn says man on Earth has lost this awareness because he has focused on devices and inventions of his own and become hypnotized by his playthings and ideas, and that through meditation it is possible totally to reduce the illusion that creates the separation to what it actually is, a total illusion."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 25-26; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsAppreciationOfReality a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation yields, very rapidly, the return to an appreciation of reality"@en, "Meditation bringt sehr rasch die Rückkehr zur Wertschätzung der Wirklichkeit hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: all of this may be very simply remedied. All that is necessary is that he individually avail himself to this appreciation of reality through the process of meditation, for this process stills his active conscious mind; very rapidly, then, he can return to an appreciation of the reality in the functioning of the real creation."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaAppreciationOfReality ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 25; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaIllusion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The illusion: physical existence as a teaching that teaches only those aware of it"@en, "Die Illusion: das physische Dasein als eine Lehre, die nur lehrt, wer sie bemerkt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The day-to-day physical existence, which the Confederation calls an illusion. Hatonn says man on Earth generated it out of desire; that it is very useful for those who wish to evolve rapidly by experiencing and using it, so that many Confederation members would desire the opportunity to be within it; that it surrounds one for the purpose of teaching and can only teach if one becomes aware of its teachings; that many souls experience it and few use it to grow; and that once one is aware of the possibility, it is necessary to take the next step and express, regardless of the potentials which affect one, the love and understanding of the Creator, as the teacher known as Jesus did."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 26-27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaRealDesire a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness of one's real desire, which is the Creator's desire, Love"@en, "Das Gewahrsein des eigenen wirklichen Verlangens, das das Verlangen des Schöpfers ist, die Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn states without exception that man receives exactly what he desires, though it seems otherwise; perhaps desire is not understood, and the understanding is not within the intellectual mind; it may be necessary to spend time in meditation to become aware of one's real desire. When one knows the Creator's desire one knows one's own, for one is one with the Creator and all His parts; that desire is that all His parts express and experience the Love that created them."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsRealDesire a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation yields the knowledge of the Creator's desire, and with it the end of questions"@en, "Meditation bringt die Kenntnis des Verlangens des Schöpfers hervor, und mit ihr das Ende der Fragen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: become aware of your Creator and of His desire; when you know His desire you will feel it; there will be no more confusion, there will be no more questions, you will have found what you have sought; you will have found Love. This may be found simply, in meditation."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: felt knowledge, the end of confusion and of questions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaRealDesire ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaIntellectualSeekingCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No interpretation of the written or spoken word will lead to the simple truth"@en, "Keine Auslegung des geschriebenen oder gesprochenen Wortes führt zur einfachen Wahrheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: no amount of seeking within the intellectual concepts of your people, no amount of careful planning or careful interpretation of the written or spoken word will lead you to the simple truth; it may be found simply, in meditation."@en ;
    skos:note "A self-warning: the book consists of written words of this kind, and the caution, quoted by the editors, places its own reading below meditation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaContactReceiving ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 27; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaLawOfConfusion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The Law of Confusion, called the Law of Free Will"@en, "Das Gesetz der Verwirrung, Gesetz des freien Willens genannt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ra calls the Law of Confusion, which the questioner has called the Law of Free Will, one of the more significant primal distortions of the Law of One. The introduction says the Confederation holds free will to be at the foundation of the universe, each entity a totally unique part of the one unity, and that its concern is always to avoid infringement upon the free will of any person, which shapes its method of contact. Ra says those who found the light/love of a density without desire for service to others have by the Law of Free Will the right to its use for whatever purpose."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 28; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 3 (January 21, 1981), pp. 84-85; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 109; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaWisdomCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Be careful of what you know: in the real creation it has power, and desire aims it"@en, "Hütet euch vor dem, was ihr wisst: in der wirklichen Schöpfung hat es Macht, und das Verlangen richtet sie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: there are pieces of information that are of importance and pieces that are not. Wisdom is a rather lonely matter, and you must accept this as you acquire the burden of wisdom. That which you know, you are to be careful of, for what you know in the real creation has power, and that which you desire is all of the direction at which that power will be aimed; but have faith in what you know and feed your faith and understanding through meditation."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 29; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaServiceToOthers a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Service to others, which is service to self"@en, "Dienst an anderen, der Dienst am Selbst ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says service to others is service to one's self, not alike but identical, since there is identity between others and ourselves, and that each person is a completely free entity whose independence must in no way be shaken. Ra says that to serve one is to serve all; that service to others results in service to self, preserving and further harmonizing the distortions of those seeking intelligent infinity through these disciplines; and that the Confederation waits for the calling."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 73; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 7 (January 25, 1981), p. 108; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 8 (January 26, 1981), p. 110; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaNegativityInService a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "A negative feeling toward another stains the service one gives"@en, "Ein negatives Gefühl gegenüber einem anderen befleckt den Dienst, den man leistet"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: that which is felt of a negative nature towards a sheep of the flock is felt towards one's self and towards the Creator; this enters the service one attempts to give to oneself and to the Creator through service to another and causes a blot or a stain upon the perfect service one would have performed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the negative feeling is named as what spoils the service; the outcome is not observable and the failure is put on the server's own feeling."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaServiceToOthers ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaReadinessToServe a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Readiness to serve: answers to all one's questions, received in meditation"@en, "Bereitschaft zum Dienst: Antworten auf alle Fragen, in der Meditation empfangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn names one thing of great importance, personal preparation for the service of one's fellow man. Through meditation one will receive answers to all one's questions, which can be reduced to an extremely simple concept; once this has been done one will be ready to serve, as others have served, qualified to reach out to one's fellow man and lead him from the darkness of confusion back into the light that he desires."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsReadinessToServe a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation yields the preparation for service"@en, "Meditation bringt die Vorbereitung zum Dienst hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: it is necessary that you prepare yourselves for this service. This of course is done in meditation; through this technique you will receive answers to all of your questions; once this has been done you will be ready to serve."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaReadinessToServe ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 30; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaProficientVocalChannel a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Proficiency as a vocal channel who receives the Confederation's thoughts readily"@en, "Gewandtheit als stimmlicher Kanal, der die Gedanken der Konföderation leicht empfängt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn says there is a need for many more channels who can receive directly the thoughts so many people are seeking, and that the Confederation is attempting to generate greater numbers of proficient vocal channels who can receive its thoughts quite readily. Rueckert says the Confederation sources greatly appreciate vocal channels trained in groups such as the one in Louisville since 1962, never suggest their message is unique, and can only perform their service through vocal channels."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 30-31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaDailyMeditationYieldsChannel a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Daily meditation, with the desire for contact, is all that is required for a vocal channel"@en, "Tägliche Meditation, mit dem Verlangen nach Kontakt, ist alles, was ein stimmlicher Kanal braucht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: this requires daily meditation. This is all that is required: daily meditation. It is assumed, of course, that as this daily meditation is performed there is a desire for our contact."@en ;
    skos:note "The only sufficiency statement in the part: one practice and one assumed desire are said to be all that is required, which makes a meditator with the desire who does not become a proficient channel a case against it. The text names no period."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaProficientVocalChannel ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSoloContactCaution a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Not to attempt Confederation contact in solitary meditation, only in a group with an experienced receiver"@en, "Keinen Kontakt zur Konföderation in einsamer Meditation versuchen, nur in einer Gruppe mit einem erfahrenen Empfänger"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert, as one who has participated in meditation groups for many years, suggests that individual meditations not include the attempt to contact Confederation sources; it is best to pursue the attempt only in a group situation, preferably a group which contains at least one experienced receiver."@en ;
    skos:note "No reason and no consequence is given; the caution is a recommendation from experience."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:RaVocalChanneling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaTuning a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Tuning before meditation: prayer, chanting, inspirational reading or the white light"@en, "Abstimmung vor der Meditation: Gebet, Gesang, erbauliche Lektüre oder das weiße Licht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rueckert strongly recommends, whether meditating alone or in a group, some means of tuning so that the meditation which follows will be at the highest spiritual level possible. It can be done in any way preferable to the meditator: the Lord's Prayer, Aum-ing or other singing or chanting, the reading of some inspirational writing, or a careful visualization of the white light of the Creator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTunedState a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The tuned state: meditation at its highest level, the instrument precisely tuned"@en, "Der abgestimmte Zustand: Meditation auf ihrer höchsten Stufe, das Instrument genau abgestimmt"@de ;
    skos:definition "For the meditator, the state in which the meditation is at the highest spiritual level possible. For the instrument, the precise tuning Ra says it had to wait for before speaking through her, because it sends a narrow band vibration, and the proper state of depth of singleness or one-pointedness it waited for again before answering a question."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 70; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 72; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaTuningYieldsTunedState a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Tuning yields meditation at the highest spiritual level possible"@en, "Abstimmung bringt Meditation auf der höchsten möglichen geistigen Stufe hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The tuning is recommended so that the meditation which follows will be at the highest spiritual level possible."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaTuning ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaTunedState ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaForgettingProcess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The forgetting process at birth into this incarnation"@en, "Der Vorgang des Vergessens bei der Geburt in diese Inkarnation"@de ;
    skos:definition "What Ra calls the forgetting process, which occurs at the time of birth into this incarnation and veils the lessons one came to learn; for a Wanderer, the love and the light the person was intended to share."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 36; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaPenetratingTheForgetting a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Penetrating the forgetting process and becoming aware of one's lessons"@en, "Den Vorgang des Vergessens durchdringen und der eigenen Lektionen gewahr werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "One of the most highly regarded fruits of meditation and seeking, the introduction says: the ability of the seeker to penetrate the forgetting process so as to become aware of the lessons to be learned during this incarnation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationYieldsPenetratingTheForgetting a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation and seeking yield the penetration of the forgetting process"@en, "Meditation und Suchen bringen das Durchdringen des Vergessens hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction counts among the most highly regarded fruits of the meditation and seeking process the ability to penetrate the forgetting process that occurs at birth."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaPenetratingTheForgetting ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 31; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaAnalyticalAvoidance a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "One's own thinking helps one avoid the lesson one wishes to learn"@en, "Das eigene Denken hilft, die Lektion zu umgehen, die man lernen will"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: when a confrontation in such a lesson has been achieved, that which separates you from understanding is most often your own thinking. Your conscious thinking processes are quite capable of being self-destructive in the sense that they may aid you to avoid the lesson you wish in reality to learn. If a temporary abeyance of the conscious, analytical processes can be achieved, you may return to the problem with a much clearer mentality, ready to learn rather than only to avoid what you came to learn."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: the lesson is not learned because analytical thought avoids it; the failure is put on the seeker's own thinking and is recognized by the repetition of the difficulty."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaLessonLearning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 31-32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaSemiMeditativeState a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Formal meditation, then a semi-meditative state of attention at all times"@en, "Förmliche Meditation, dann jederzeit ein halbmeditativer Zustand der Aufmerksamkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn, knowing how difficult it is to achieve the meditative state at all times, urges dependence on meditation of a formal kind and then the attempt at a semi-meditative state at all times, by which he means simply a state of attention."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaSemiMeditativeStateYieldsLessons a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "The semi-meditative state keeps destructive impulses from blocking the lessons"@en, "Der halbmeditative Zustand hält zerstörerische Regungen davon ab, die Lektionen zu verstellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state of attention is to be kept so that one's destructive impulses are not free to clog the mind completely and keep one from learning the lessons one came to learn."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaSemiMeditativeState ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaLessonLearning ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmp:RaMeditationOnUnity a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Meditating upon the complete unity of oneself and all one sees, especially in difficulty"@en, "Über die vollständige Einheit des Selbst mit allem Gesehenen meditieren, besonders in Schwierigkeiten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: meditate upon the complete unity of yourself and all that you see; do this not once, and not simply in present circumstances, but at all times, and especially in difficult circumstances; keep your mind stayed upon the unity of the Creator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaAlleviationByUnity a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alleviation of difficult circumstances by loving and feeling at one with them"@en, "Linderung schwieriger Umstände, indem man sie liebt und sich eins mit ihnen fühlt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Insofar as one loves and feels at one with the things that are difficult, to that extent those circumstances are alleviated. Hatonn attributes this not to any law within the physical illusion but to the Law of Love: the spiritual body, interpenetrated with the physical body, is higher than it, and the changes one makes by love upon the spiritual body of necessity reflect themselves within the physical illusion. Even if the universe of those around remains disharmonious, one's own universe will become harmonious, not by one's own doing but by the love of the Creator."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaMeditationOnUnityYieldsAlleviation a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Meditation on unity yields the alleviation of difficult circumstances"@en, "Meditation über die Einheit bringt die Linderung schwieriger Umstände hervor"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: insofar as you love and feel at one with those things which are difficult for you, to that extent will those circumstances be alleviated; if your mind is stayed upon the unity of the Creator, your own universe will become harmonious."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a sign of success: circumstances alleviated and one's own universe harmonious, in proportion to the love."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:RaMeditationOnUnity ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:RaAlleviationByUnity ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 32; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaClingingToThirdDensity a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No precise prediction of the Earth changes, and no time spent on preserving third-density existence"@en, "Keine genaue Vorhersage der Erdveränderungen, und keine Zeit für den Erhalt des Daseins in der dritten Dichte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: it is neither permissible nor possible for us to tell you precisely what events will occur or when, because the vibration within the mind and heart of the peoples of the planet is determining and will determine the precise events; there is karma within the planet that must be adjusted as the cycle changes. The rain, wind and fire will destroy only things of the third density; spend no time concerning yourselves with maintaining your third-density existence after the vibration change to fourth density has been completed. If your graduation day has come, what is necessary for your emergence into fourth density will be done for you by helpers. You cling to the physical body as though your spirit were attached permanently to it; the spirit resides within a shell, and the spirit does not perish."@en ;
    skos:note "A refusal to predict given with its reason, which is also a caution against reading the passage as a prediction."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaHarvest ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 33-34; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHarvest a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The harvest at the end of a cycle"@en, "Die Ernte am Ende eines Zyklus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The introduction calls the harvest a Judgment Day in which the one who judges is not a God apart but the God within; some go on to a new age of love and light in a positive density, others repeat the grade and relearn the lessons of love, and Hatonn calls the Confederation the Harvesters, attempting to increase by a relatively small percentage the number harvested into the path of love and understanding. Ra says that those who finish a cycle of experience are separated by their own choice into the vibratory distortion most comfortable to them, a process watched by nurturing beings; the spirit complex of each harvested entity moves along the line of light until the light grows too glaring, and there stops. A major cycle is approximately 25,000 years; those who have progressed may be harvested at the end of three, approximately 75,000 to 76,000 years, and all are harvested at that end regardless of progress, because the planet has moved through the useful part of the dimension. Ra says the planetary changes are very trivial and that it does not concern itself with the conditions which bring about harvest, and that an estimate of the percentage to be harvested is meaningless because the harvesting is not yet."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 34-35; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 1 (January 15, 1981), p. 72; read in a full-text layer of that edition", "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), session 6 (January 24, 1981), pp. 99-101; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaHarvestThreshold a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "A vibratory rate above a certain minimal level before the harvest into the path of love"@en, "Eine Schwingungsrate über einem bestimmten Mindestmaß vor der Ernte in den Pfad der Liebe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: the choice is measured by the vibratory rate of the individual; it is necessary, if an individual is to join those who make the choice of love and understanding, for his rate of vibration to be above a certain minimal level. Many are close to it but, through continuing erroneous thought, fluctuate around it or drift away; many are high enough to travel with no difficulty into the coming density. Those above the level have already made the grade; those far below it cannot be helped by the Confederation at this time."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a minimal level is named as threshold, but not quantified in this part; the failure is put on the individual's thought, and the outcome, repeating the grade, is not observable within the life."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:RaHarvest ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:RaVibratoryRate ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Those not above the level are not harvested into the path of love and understanding and will have to repeat this particular grade of lessons and relearn the lessons of love (Introduction, p. 35)." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, pp. 34-35; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

pmc:RaVerbalChoice a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The verbal choice means nothing: the choice is measured by its demonstration"@en, "Die ausgesprochene Wahl bedeutet nichts: die Wahl wird an ihrer Darlegung gemessen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hatonn: each person on Earth will shortly make a choice, with no middle area, between the path of love and light and the other. The choice will not be made by saying I choose the path of love and light or I do not choose it; the verbal choice will mean nothing. It will be measured by the individual's demonstration of his choice, which the Confederation interprets easily, as his vibratory rate."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a condition of failure: a declared choice without its demonstration is named as void; the failure is put on the individual's conduct."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:RaHarvest ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:RaMaterial ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TheRaMaterialBookOne ;
    dcterms:source "The Law of One, Book I: The Ra Material (Louisville: L/L Research, 1984), Introduction, p. 34; read in a full-text layer of that edition" .

